  "description": "An oil painting of a harbour laid on in thick strokes over a smooth underpainting, each stroke with its own lit ridge, grooves and a second colour mixed in wet. The strokes drift with the swell and the wind, and every section is painted at its own hour, from dawn through golden afternoon to a moonlit night, with a slow push in. Headlines are laid on a brushed ground with a stroke under them, charts are poured, painters wave brushes and jars fill. Between sections one loaded yellow brush is dragged across and reveals the next.",
